2. Delivery Performance
  Lateness Days (days_for_shipping_real - days_for_shipment_scheduled)
  Mean = 0.56 days
  Median = 1 day
  Min = -2 (delivered earlier)
  Max = 4 (delayed up to 4 days)
Insight: Most orders are delivered on time or within 1 day delay.
Late Delivery Risk by Shipping Mode:
| Shipping Mode  | Late Risk (%) |
| -------------- | ------------- |
| First Class    | **95%**       |
| Second Class   | **77%**       |
| Same Day       | **46%**       |
| Standard Class | **38%**       |

Interesting finding: First Class has the highest late risk, which may suggest that late_delivery_risk is a flag generated differently from actual lateness days.

3. Profitability & Discount
  Profit Margin (order_profit_per_order / sales)
  Mean = 11%
  Median = 24%
  Min = -275% (heavy losses on some orders)
  Max = 50%
  Std = 0.42 (large variability)
  Correlation with Discount Rate: ≈ -0.02 (very weak overall)
Reason: majority of orders have discount_rate = 0.
Filtering only discounted orders would likely reveal a stronger negative relationship.

4. Categorical Features
  Shipping Mode: 4 categories (Standard, First, Second, Same Day) — distribution is unbalanced, Standard dominates.
  Market / Region: multiple regions; a few dominate the dataset.
  Category Name: includes Furniture, Technology, Office Supplies (similar to Superstore data).
  Customer Segment: distributed across Consumer, Corporate, Home Office.

